// Chuck: noisy novice bravado, kept playful without punching down.

characterChat "Chuck" {
	chat entergame {
		"Chuck just showed up. This place is officially louder."
		"All right, who put me near the dangerous equipment?"
		"I'm ready enough. Somebody point me at the action."
		"Chuck reporting for trouble, probably the manageable kind."
		"I brought confidence. The skill should arrive any minute."
		"Let's make some noise before Dalton takes all the credit."
		"Fresh match, fresh chance to look like I planned this."
		"I'm in. Try not to start without the entertainment."
	}
	chat levelstart {
		"$map, huh? I can get lost here with real enthusiasm."
		"Find a weapon, find a target, avoid the obvious holes. Easy."
		"I call the loud route through the middle."
		"Corners first, bragging second. I do learn."
		"If anyone needs me, follow the unnecessary shouting."
		"This layout looks simple from exactly one spot."
		"Let's see which hallway makes the best entrance."
		"Plan for $map: keep moving until it looks intentional."
	}
	chat kill {
		"Ha! Chuck one, reasonable expectations zero."
		"The $weapon and I finally agreed on something."
		"Got you, $other. Yes, I'm surprised too."
		"That absolutely counted as tactical."
		"Somebody remember that shot exactly the way I describe it."
		"I knew where you were. Eventually."
		"Turns out confidence does help the aim a little."
		"Down you go. Chuck is having a moment."
	}
	chat killWrench {
		"Wrench delivery! No signature required."
		"That was close enough to hear my brilliant plan."
		"Tools out, dignity gone, point secured."
		"I fixed the problem, $other. Very hands-on work."
		"The wrench chose violence and I respected the decision."
		"You got within swinging distance. That's on both of us."
		"No ammunition, no problem, plenty of noise."
		"Chuck's repair service has extremely firm policies."
	}
	chat killStreak {
		"Three! I may have accidentally become dangerous."
		"Keep count for me; this is getting impressive."
		"That's a streak. Nobody touch anything."
		"I am on fire, figuratively, which is the good version."
		"Three in a row! Dalton better be watching."
		"The plan is working, so I refuse to explain it."
		"Chuck momentum is real and poorly supervised."
		"Another one down. This confidence has evidence now."
	}
	chat revenge {
		"There you are, $other. I saved that complaint for you."
		"Payback delivered with extra volume."
		"That's for making me look briefly less amazing."
		"I remembered the face and almost remembered the route."
		"Score settled. Grudge storage is empty again."
		"You had your turn; Chuck just took his."
		"I came back with a louder answer."
		"Revenge works better when I stop missing."
	}
	chat death {
		"Okay, $other, that one got my attention."
		"The $weapon wins this argument. For now."
		"I was doing great right up to the important part."
		"Somebody tell Dalton I nearly had that."
		"Fine shot. I object to the result."
		"Chuck down! Please hold the applause."
		"I found the dangerous end of that corridor."
		"That plan needed one more rehearsal."
	}
	chat deathAccident {
		"Nobody saw that, and nobody needs to."
		"The floor and I have a serious disagreement."
		"That button was much more committed than expected."
		"I meant to discover exactly where not to stand."
		"Chuck versus basic caution: caution takes the round."
		"That shortcut had a very sudden ending."
		"No opponent required; I handled the mistake myself."
		"Resetting with slightly more respect for edges."
	}
	chat itemDenied {
		"Hey, $other, I was loudly heading toward that $item."
		"You took the pickup and my whole developing strategy."
		"Fine, keep the $item. I'll improvise something noisier."
		"I arrived exactly one bad decision too late."
		"That resource was almost definitely mine in spirit."
		"Pickup gone. Backup plan currently loading."
		"You beat me there; I was busy making an entrance."
		"Next cycle, I'm racing first and talking second."
	}
	chat leadTaken {
		"Chuck is leading! Check the board before it changes."
		"First place looks surprisingly good from here."
		"I have the lead and several questions about how."
		"Everybody remain calm; I am somehow in front."
		"This scoreboard finally understands raw potential."
		"Top spot secured by nerve, noise, and favorable timing."
		"I'm ahead. Dalton is never hearing the end of this."
		"The Chuck era begins now and may be quite brief."
	}
	chat leadLost {
		"Well, the scoreboard corrected itself. Rude."
		"Somebody slipped ahead while I was celebrating."
		"Temporary setback; permanent commentary."
		"I lost first place, not the ability to shout about it."
		"The lead moved. Chuck is moving after it."
		"All right, back to the ambitious part of the plan."
		"Somebody borrowed my spot at the top."
		"I can recover this if the walls stop interfering."
	}
	chat matchWin {
		"Victory! Exactly as I confidently revised the plan."
		"Chuck takes the match and a completely reasonable bow."
		"Good game. I made the important parts look exciting."
		"We won! I will be available for exaggerated retellings."
		"That result deserves snacks and several victory laps."
		"Top result, full volume, no further questions."
		"I knew we had it somewhere around the final score."
		"Great fight. Chuck officially approves this outcome."
	}
	chat matchLose {
		"Good game. My victory speech can wait one round."
		"You got it this time; I supplied the atmosphere."
		"That loss was educational in several inconvenient ways."
		"All right, fair win. Rematch after I regroup."
		"The score says no, but my confidence remains confused."
		"I can play better than that and probably quieter."
		"No excuses. Well, none worth saying out loud."
		"Fair match. Next one gets the improved Chuck."
	}
	chat farewell {
		"Chuck is heading out. The volume should drop shortly."
		"Good games. Try not to enjoy the silence too much."
		"I'm off before Dalton invents another round."
		"That's enough heroics for one session."
		"See you next match, preferably from a safer distance."
		"Later, everyone. Remember the impressive parts."
		"Chuck signing off with dignity mostly intact."
		"I'm gone. Keep the place noisy for me."
	}
	reply help {
		priority 40
		source any
		addressed either
		trigger "help me"
		trigger "need help"
		trigger "medic"
		trigger "need a medic"
		trigger "need health"
		trigger "need armor"
		trigger "cover me"
		trigger "need backup"
		"Hang on, $other. Chuck assistance is approaching loudly."
		"Get behind cover; I'll create a very obvious distraction."
		"I'm coming. Keep breathing and keep your head down."
		"Backup requested, backup attempting to find the route."
	}
	reply goodGame {
		priority 30
		source any
		addressed either
		trigger "gg"
		trigger "ggwp"
		trigger "good game"
		trigger "great game"
		trigger "good match"
		trigger "great match"
		trigger "well played"
		trigger "good games"
		"Good game, $other. That had exactly enough chaos."
		"Yeah, well played. Chuck rates it highly."
		"Solid match. I even learned part of $map."
		"Great game; let's claim every mistake was entertainment."
	}
	reply challenge {
		priority 25
		source any
		addressed either
		trigger "bring it"
		trigger "come get me"
		trigger "fight me"
		trigger "try me"
		trigger "come on then"
		trigger "you suck"
		trigger "noob"
		trigger "ez"
		"Big talk, $other. Conveniently, I brought big talk too."
		"Challenge accepted before good judgment arrives."
		"Come on, then. Chuck has momentum to manufacture."
		"You want a fight? I can provide an enthusiastic one."
	}
	reply greeting {
		priority 20
		source any
		addressed either
		trigger "hi"
		trigger "hello"
		trigger "hey"
		trigger "greetings"
		trigger "good morning"
		trigger "good evening"
		trigger "howdy"
		trigger "yo"
		"Hey, $other! Chuck has entered the conversation."
		"Hello there. Ready for some questionable excellence?"
		"Howdy! Glad somebody friendly found me."
		"Greetings from the loud side of $map."
	}
	reply thanks {
		priority 20
		source any
		addressed either
		trigger "thanks"
		trigger "thank you"
		trigger "thx"
		trigger "ty"
		trigger "much appreciated"
		trigger "cheers"
		trigger "thanks a lot"
		trigger "thank you very much"
		"You're welcome, $other. I accept applause too."
		"No problem. Chuck service comes with extra commentary."
		"Any time; that went better than expected."
		"Glad to help. Please remember the competent part."
	}
	reply praise {
		priority 20
		source any
		addressed either
		trigger "nice shot"
		trigger "good shot"
		trigger "great shot"
		trigger "nice kill"
		trigger "good kill"
		trigger "nice one"
		trigger "well done"
		trigger "good work"
		"Finally, a witness with excellent judgment."
		"Thanks, $other. I practiced that for nearly seconds."
		"Appreciated! The confidence was doing heavy work."
		"Nice of you to notice; I'll mention it repeatedly."
	}
	reply apology {
		priority 20
		source any
		addressed either
		trigger "sorry"
		trigger "my bad"
		trigger "apologies"
		trigger "oops"
		trigger "whoops"
		trigger "forgive me"
		trigger "didn't mean that"
		trigger "pardon me"
		"We're fine, $other. I've made louder mistakes."
		"Apology accepted; let's call it experimental movement."
		"No hard feelings. Just warn me before the next surprise."
		"All good. Chuck carries no grudge longer than one respawn."
	}
	reply farewell {
		priority 20
		source any
		addressed either
		trigger "bye"
		trigger "goodbye"
		trigger "good night"
		trigger "gtg"
		trigger "gotta go"
		trigger "see ya"
		trigger "see you later"
		trigger "later"
		"Later, $other. Leave some excitement for next time."
		"Good night. Chuck will resume the noise another day."
		"See you around; travel with fewer shortcuts than I do."
		"Take care. I'll save a dramatic entrance for your return."
	}
	reply direct {
		priority 0
		source any
		addressed required
		trigger "Chuck"
		trigger "hey Chuck"
		trigger "Chuck help"
		trigger "Chuck hello"
		trigger "Chuck listen"
		trigger "Chuck there"
		trigger "Chuck answer"
		trigger "Chuck wait"
		"Chuck here, $other. What's happening?"
		"You called the right loud person. Go ahead."
		"I'm listening, which is new and important."
		"Say it quick before I improve the story."
	}
}
